# Task 5 - Task 5 – Text Vectorization using TF-IDF

1. TF-IDF (Term Frequency–Inverse Document Frequency) was used to convert the text data into numerical features.
2. The cleaned TED Talk text was used for vectorization to represent the content of each talk.
3. The dataset contains **3,921 usable TED Talks** with 24 columns.
4. A maximum of 5,000 text features was selected during TF-IDF vectorization.
5. The TF-IDF matrix was successfully generated with a shape of **(3921, 5000)**.
6. Cosine similarity was calculated to measure the similarity between different TED Talks.
7. The similarity matrix was successfully generated with a shape of **(3921, 3921)**.
8. Talks with similar words and topics receive higher similarity scores, helping the recommendation system identify related TED Talks.
9. TF-IDF helps the system focus on important words while reducing the importance of frequently occurring common words.
10. The generated TF-IDF vectors and cosine similarity scores can be used in the next stage to recommend relevant TED Talks to users.

## Final Conclusion

Text vectorization using TF-IDF was successfully completed. The cleaned TED Talk text was converted into numerical vectors, and cosine similarity was calculated for all 3,921 talks. These results provide the foundation for building a content-based TED Talks Recommendation System.